int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\cdot ⟨6,\\,-2,\\,-4⟩-⟨3,\\,5,\\,-7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12,\\,-4,\\,-8⟩-⟨3,\\,5,\\,-7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,\\,-9,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440628 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440628 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129273" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440628 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440628 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate \n${\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨6,\\,-2,\\,4⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{4}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨3,\\,-1,\\,2⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440628 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0dd4df5a-0e6b-52af-bfbd-9f8a6a0eb73b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440628 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{4}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨3,\\,-1,\\,2⟩-⟨6,\\,-2,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-9,\\,3,\\,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440629 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440629 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129293" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440629 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440629 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${\\int }_{1}^{5}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=i-j+3\\,k$ \nand \n$c=2\\,i-k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440629 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "42e2902f-b402-5b6e-826c-93f62fddd9ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440629 #edb/ref 1074 "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(2\\,i-k)\\times (i-j+3\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0-1)i-(6+1)j+(-2-0)k \\\\  & =-i-7\\,j-2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440630 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440630 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129271" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440630 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440630 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨15,\\,3,\\,6⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨12,\\,2,\\,4⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440630 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "47592607-bdfd-5d8e-9c5b-5217893655c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440630 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨15,\\,3,\\,6⟩-⟨12,\\,2,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440631 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440631 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129151" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440631 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440631 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate ${\\int }_{1}^{2}[f(t)+\\frac{5}{3}g(t)]\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,1,\\,4⟩$ and ${\\int }_{1}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-3,\\,6,\\,0⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440631 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8fc5a0e9-33d2-5427-a227-a63b18c415e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440631 #edb/ref 1074 "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}[f(t)+\\frac{5}{3}g(t)]\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{5}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[f(t)+\\frac{5}{3}g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{5}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,1,\\,4⟩+\\frac{5}{3}⟨-3,\\,6,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,1,\\,4⟩+⟨-5,\\,10,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7,\\,11,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440632 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440632 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129288" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440632 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440632 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that \n${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{e}{2}\\,i+3e\\,j-\\,k,$ \n$c=4\\,i-j+u\\,k,$\nand \n${\\int }_{1}^{3}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ what is the value of $u?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440632 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "90fd82d6-81fe-5d91-84c9-583a4bc9e1c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440632 #edb/ref 1074 "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(4\\,i-j+u\\,k)\\cdot (\\frac{e}{2}\\,i+3e\\,j-k) \\\\  & =2e-3e-u \\\\  & =-e-u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${\\int }_{1}^{3}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ we must have $-e-u=0,$ which means that $u=-e.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440633 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440633 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32496" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440633 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440633 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}[6f(t)-2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,-\\frac{2}{3},\\,3⟩$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440633 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "936ae073-f786-5498-b379-ef3a0cdfd96d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440633 #edb/ref 1074 "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}[6f(t)-2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=6{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[6f(t)-2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =6{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,-\\frac{2}{3},\\,3⟩-2⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-4,\\,18⟩-⟨2,\\,2,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-6,\\,16⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440634 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440634 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129296" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440634 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440634 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=7\\,i-4\\,j-k$ \nand \n$c=3\\,i-5\\,j+2\\,k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440634 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9dfd8a34-cf86-59cc-aba6-9a0a73cfe2af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440634 #edb/ref 1074 "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(3\\,i-5\\,j+2\\,k)\\times (7\\,i-4\\,j-k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 7 & -4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(5+8)i-(-3-14)j+(-12+35)k \\\\  & =13\\,i+17\\,j+23\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
